From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ClodoCapeo <159788250+ClodoCapeo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(libobs): remove initial GPU encode frame delay

The texture encoder worker already waits on the keyed texture synchronization
before submitting to the encoder.  Skipping the first semaphore wake adds one
60 fps cadence to the handoff without providing an additional synchronization
guarantee.  Start processing the first ready texture immediately.

All encoder settings, quality controls, audio paths, and the asynchronous
worker architecture remain unchanged.

Agent-Role: eleven

Agent-Thread: 01a045e2-996f-7913-99f0-2cd237d3a6f8

Work-Unit: pulsar-nvenc-gpu-handoff-fastpath-20260902

Issue: fastpath-no-issue

ADR-Revision: amendment-1-draft-r1-ac12-boundaries-20260831

Evidence: NUM_ENCODE_TEXTURE_FRAMES_TO_WAIT was 1; keyed texture sync remains
the readiness barrier for every GPU texture.
---
 libobs/obs-internal.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libobs/obs-internal.h b/libobs/obs-internal.h
index d88093eec..b7241eb6e 100644
--- a/libobs/obs-internal.h
+++ b/libobs/obs-internal.h
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@
 #define NUM_CHANNELS 3
 #define MICROSECOND_DEN 1000000
 #define NUM_ENCODE_TEXTURES 10
-#define NUM_ENCODE_TEXTURE_FRAMES_TO_WAIT 1
+#define NUM_ENCODE_TEXTURE_FRAMES_TO_WAIT 0
 
 static inline int64_t packet_dts_usec(struct encoder_packet *packet)
 {

